title: 'Decided: the request keeps its name, "set overrides followed", and takes "next" or a perspective''s name.'
pid: ecb4a8a1-4d97-49f9-97a8-ef99f2f6375d
body: |2-
  Only the user-facing names became Jeff's word, "perspective"; the
  wire, the server's types and the buffers' variables still say
  "overrides followed", since they name what a perspective is, and a
  rename would touch every client for nothing they do. The glossary
  entry "perspective" ties the two. The names on the wire: "root
  authors", "user", "owner of NAME". A save may name any of them, not
  only those in the cycle; a request to switch may name one in the
  cycle, as skg-for-ai does, while the clients always send "next".
